{"clock":1,"nonce":"5cb60722fec3d46aab023b8d81144a40","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793814049,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6208108486"},"data":{"body":"Found writing the user manual (PR #86).\n\n**Now.** `@me` in a filter or an assignment means your *forge login*. On a board that never synced with a forge, `git board set \u003cid\u003e assignee=+@me` and `ls \"involves:@me\"` fail: \"@me needs your forge login\". For a product whose point is independence from forges, that's backwards.\n\n**Want.** `@me` resolves to the person you write as (`board.me`): their forge login where they have one on the issue's forge, else their name. Assignee labels on a forge-less board name people by name (`assignee:ada`), and the sync maps a name to the forge login when the person has an account there.\n\n**Acceptance.** On a fresh board with no forge: `git board me --new`, then `set \u003cid\u003e assignee=+@me` and `ls involves:@me` work; after a GitHub sync, the label maps to the GitHub login.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_","title":"cli: @me without a forge: resolve to the person you write as"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793822095,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6208108486"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793822095,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6208108486"},"data":{"add":["feat"],"remove":null}}]}